      "question": {
        ":question/id": "31bb183b-56f8-5b41-a2b9-ec55651175e4",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
        ":question/problem": "If $f(x)=\\frac{{e}^{x}}{\\cos x},$ find ${f}^{\\prime}(x).$",
        ":question/worked-solution": "In this case, the expression for $f(x)$ is a quotient $\\frac{u(x)}{v(x)}$ with $u(x)={e}^{x}$ and $v(x)=\\cos x.$ \n\nTherefore, we apply the quotient rule as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{\\prime}(x)&=\\frac{u^{\\prime}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot v^{\\prime}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{(e^{x})^{\\prime}\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})-(e^{x})\\cdot (\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{\\prime}}{(\\cos{\\left(x \\right)})^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{{e}^{x}\\cos x+{e}^{x}\\sin x}{(\\cos x)^{2}}\\\\ &=\\frac{{e}^{x}(\\cos x+\\sin x)}{\\cos^{2}x}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
        ":question/answer-fields": [
          {
            ":answer-field/id": "4328681c-5f26-5840-a235-44132c2c0ca2",
            ":answer-field/key": "selection",
